# The build context is streamed to the docker daemon on EVERY build, including every
# scripts/worker_build.sh run. Without this, ~0.5 GB of untracked local Tika checkouts
# (.tika-src 292M, .tika-fixed 100M, .tika-baseline 99M) plus .git goes over the wire each
# time, on what is meant to be an inner-loop test command.
#
# Nothing here is a build input FOR THE CLONING IMAGES: Dockerfile.localtika and friends take
# Tika from their own tika-build stage at the pinned SHA, not from the context.
#
# The exception is Dockerfile.default.localsrc, which builds from a local checkout and so
# genuinely needs .tika-src. Excluding it here broke that image outright ("/.tika-src": not
# found). It carries its own Dockerfile.default.localsrc.dockerignore, which BuildKit prefers
# over this file. If you add an exclusion here, add it there too -- BuildKit replaces this
# list rather than merging with it.
.git
.tika-src/
.tika-fixed/
.tika-baseline/
worker_jvm/target/
**/__pycache__/
.venv/
*.ext4
